  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation is on an explicit function with a body, `impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Domain]/fn[node_content]`. That is a permitted target. The justification is in fenced citation commentary, and it is substantive and matches the source.\n\n- `Domain::node_content` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` (`trait[Domain]/fn[node_content]`) has no default body. The test's `Domain` impl therefore has to define it, as the commentary says.\n- The body is `panic!(\"edge inspection must not read node contents\")`. This is an intentional guard. Reaching it would fail the test, so zero execution is expected and acceptable.\n- The enclosing test `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` asserts only `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` selection dependencies, which matches the claim that the records assert selection dependencies only. It never supplies node contents.\n\nI found no gap.",
